;; orders/cancel.aura
;; Cancels a previously placed order.
;;
;; In the checkout pipeline, an order can be in one of a few states:
;;   - committed   (money captured, inventory reserved)
;;   - compensated (saga rolled back; nothing to do)
;;   - pending     (placed but not yet finalized)
;;
;; This module is the high-level "cancel" entry point that *retrospectively*
;; voids an already-committed order. It is distinct from saga compensation,
;; which rolls back a partially-completed pipeline: cancellation here assumes
;; a successful checkout that the caller now wants to undo.
;;
;; Required exported API:
;;   (api-cancel-order state) -> cancel-result
;;
;; The function performs the following steps:
;;   1. Read the order id and payment-auth-id off the state. If there is
;;      no auth id (e.g. the order never reached the authorize stage),
;;      cancellation is a no-op and returns (list 'CANCELED 'no-auth).
;;   2. Read the cancel-reason if one was recorded by the caller.
;;   3. Call api-void-payment on the stored auth id to release the hold
;;      on the customer's funds. We always void, never refund, because
;;      cancellation here targets authorized-but-not-yet-captured holds
;;      and the orchestrator's commit path captures *after* any cancel
;;      decision is made; in the cancel path we simply unwind.
;;   4. Mark the state as canceled by stamping 'canceled on it and
;;      recording the void id under 'payment-void-id so downstream
;;      observers (and the stdout contract, if it ever surfaces cancel
;;      output) can read it.
;;   5. Return a small cancel-result list:
;;        (list 'CANCELED auth-id void-id reason)
;;      so callers can pattern-match on the leading 'CANCELED symbol
;;      without having to know the internal layout.
;;
;; This module deliberately does NOT touch fraud or inventory stages;
;; those are handled by their own rollback paths. Cancellation is a
;; payment-focused operation: release the hold, mark the order
;; canceled, return.

(define (api-cancel-order state)
  ;; Pull the auth id off the state. If it's missing, there's nothing
  ;; to cancel -- the order never reached authorization.
  (let ((auth-id (api-state-get state 'payment-auth-id)))
    (cond
      ((or (null? auth-id) (not auth-id))
       ;; No auth id means no hold to release. Still mark the state so
       ;; subsequent pipeline runs see the cancel attempt, but signal
       ;; it via a distinct result symbol.
       (begin
         (api-state-set! state 'canceled #t)
         (api-state-set! state 'cancel-reason 'no-auth)
         (list 'CANCELED 'no-auth)))
      (else
       ;; We have a hold to release. Void it.
       (let ((void-id (api-void-payment auth-id))
             (reason (api-state-get state 'cancel-reason)))
         ;; Stamp the state so subsequent observers know the order
         ;; was canceled, not committed or compensated.
         (api-state-set! state 'canceled #t)
         (api-state-set! state 'payment-void-id void-id)
         ;; If no reason was pre-recorded, attribute it to 'unspecified
         ;; so the returned result is always a 4-element list.
         (list 'CANCELED
               auth-id
               void-id
               (if (or (null? reason) (not reason))
                   'unspecified
                   reason)))))))
